## Homepage (index.html) — Special Rules

The homepage is a draggable desktop UI. It has completely different rules from all other pages.

### Two-world model
Desktop (>768px): `.canvas` is visible, `.mobile-view` is hidden. Everything is position:absolute.
Mobile (≤768px): `.canvas` is hidden, `.mobile-view` is visible. Normal document flow.
These two worlds are fully independent. Never try to make them share layout.

### Position system — NEVER break these rules
- initPositions(), applyPositions(), updateFractions() must ALWAYS be globally scoped — never inside the if (window.innerWidth > 768) block
- initPositions() runs on load before anything else touches elements
- NEVER add a second window.addEventListener('resize', ...) — use the existing one
- wasDesktop flag must be set on window load, not at script parse time
- Inline style="top:Xpx; left:Ypx" on .retro-window and .pixel-object elements are converted to viewport fractions automatically — no extra steps needed when repositioning

### Adding a new desktop card
Give it: id, class="retro-window card-window", inline style with top/left px, transform:rotate(Xdeg)
It gets picked up by makeDraggable automatically — no JS changes needed.

```html
<a href="page.html" class="retro-window card-window" id="win-NEW" style="top:400px;left:500px;z-index:8;transform:rotate(1deg);text-decoration:none;color:inherit;">
  <div class="window-titlebar">
    <span class="window-title">case-study &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2025</span>
    <span class="window-close">×</span>
  </div>
  <div class="card-image-area">
    <img src="images/your-image.png" alt="" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;">
    <div class="card-hover-reveal">
      <div>
        <div class="card-hover-label">Tag · Tag · Tag</div>
        <div class="card-hover-name">Company</div>
        <div class="card-hover-type">Year</div>
        <div class="card-hover-title">Project Title</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-hover-footer">
        <span></span><span class="card-hover-arrow">→</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <span class="card-pill">Read Case Study</span>
  </div>
</a>
```

### Adding a new mobile carousel card
Add inside .carousel-track in the mobile-view section. Order = left-to-right display order.

```html
<a href="page.html" class="mobile-card">
  <div class="window-titlebar"><span class="window-title">case-study</span><span class="window-close">×</span></div>
  <div class="mobile-card-image"><img src="images/your-image.png" alt="" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;"></div>
  <div class="mobile-card-body">
    <div class="mobile-card-name">Project Title</div>
    <div class="mobile-card-type">Type · Company</div>
    <span class="mobile-card-arrow">→</span>
  </div>
</a>
```

No JS changes needed. When you add a card, add it in BOTH places — desktop canvas AND mobile carousel.

### Homepage never-do list
- Never add a second resize event listener
- Never move initPositions/applyPositions/updateFractions inside the mobile JS guard
- Never use position:fixed on canvas cards
- Never try to stack desktop cards vertically on mobile — use the separate mobile-card instead
- Never remove the !important flags from the 768px media query
- Never target .card-window in CSS without checking it won't affect .mobile-card
